\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 A retail company is exploring machine learning algorithms to improve its customer segmentation systems. The data science team is evaluating both K-Means and K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) algorithms but needs to understand the key differences between them, since understanding these distinctions will help the team choose the right algorithm for their specific tasks.\cb1 \
\cb3 Given this context, what do you recommend to the company?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 K-Means is a supervised learning algorithm used for classification, while KNN is an unsupervised learning algorithm used for clustering\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 K-Means requires labeled data to form clusters, whereas KNN does not use labeled data for making predictions\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 Your answer is correct
\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \strokec10 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb11 \strokec2 K-Means is an unsupervised learning algorithm used for clustering data points into groups, while KNN is a supervised learning algorithm used for classifying data points based on their proximity to labeled examples\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 K-Means is primarily used for regression tasks, while KNN is used for reducing the dimensionality of data\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 K-Means is an unsupervised learning algorithm used for clustering data points into groups, while KNN is a supervised learning algorithm used for classifying data points based on their proximity to labeled examples
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 K-Means is an unsupervised learning algorithm used to partition a dataset into distinct clusters by minimizing the variance within each cluster. KNN, on the other hand, is a supervised learning algorithm that classifies new data points based on the majority class among its k-nearest neighbors in the training data.\cb1 \
\cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 K-Means is a supervised learning algorithm used for classification, while KNN is an unsupervised learning algorithm used for clustering
\f1\b0 \'a0- K-Means is an unsupervised learning algorithm, and KNN is a supervised learning algorithm.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 K-Means requires labeled data to form clusters, whereas KNN does not use labeled data for making predictions
\f1\b0 \'a0- K-Means does not require labeled data; it is used for clustering. KNN, however, requires labeled data for classification.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 K-Means is primarily used for regression tasks, while KNN is used for reducing the dimensionality of data
\f1\b0 \'a0- K-Means is not used for regression tasks, and KNN is not primarily used for dimensionality reduction. KNN is used for classification and regression tasks based on proximity to neighbors.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
