\cf2 \cb7 Correct options:\cb1 \
\cb7 Unsupervised learning algorithms train on unlabeled data. They scan through new data and establish meaningful connections between the unknown input and predetermined outputs. For instance, unsupervised learning algorithms could group news articles from different news sites into common categories like sports and crime.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Clustering
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Clustering is an unsupervised learning technique that groups certain data inputs, so they may be categorized as a whole. There are various types of clustering algorithms depending on the input data. An example of clustering is identifying different types of network traffic to predict potential security incidents.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Dimensionality reduction
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Dimensionality reduction is an unsupervised learning technique that reduces the number of features in a dataset. It\'92s often used to preprocess data for other machine learning functions and reduce complexity and overheads. For example, it may blur out or crop background features in an image recognition application.\cb1 \
\
