\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Feature extraction involves selecting the most relevant features from the dataset, while feature selection involves creating new features from existing data\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Feature extraction and feature selection are both used to remove irrelevant features but do not reduce the dimensionality of the dataset\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Feature extraction is only applicable to supervised learning, while feature selection is only applicable to unsupervised learning\cb1 \
