\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Feature extraction reduces the number of features by transforming data into a new space, while feature selection reduces the number of features by selecting the most relevant ones from the existing features
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Feature extraction involves transforming the data into a new feature space, often using techniques like Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to reduce the number of features. Feature selection, on the other hand, involves selecting a subset of the most relevant features from the original dataset, typically using methods like forward selection, backward elimination, or regularization techniques.\cb1 \
