\pard\pardeftab720\sa383\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Real-time inference processes data in large batches at scheduled intervals, while batch inference processes individual data points immediately as they arrive
\f1\b0 \'a0- Real-time inference processes individual data points as they arrive, providing immediate predictions. Batch inference processes data in large batches at scheduled intervals.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Batch inference follows an API-based invocation, whereas real-time inference follows a schedule-based invocation
\f1\b0 \'a0- For real-time inference, the typical invocation modes are - REST API, gRPC, WebSockets, and Serverless Functions. For batch inference, the typical invocation modes are - Batch processing frameworks (Spark, Flink, Hadoop), Cloud Batch Services (AWS Batch), and scripted jobs on a schedule.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Batch inference follows a synchronous execution mode, whereas real-time inference follows an asynchronous execution mode
\f1\b0 \'a0- The execution modes for real-time inference vs batch inference are reversed in this option, so it is incorrect.\cb1 \
