\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \strokec10 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb11 \strokec2 Overfitting occurs when the model is overly complex and captures noise or random fluctuations in the training data rather than the underlying patterns\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Overfitting occurs when the model is using fewer feature combinations\cb1 \
