\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb17 \strokec2 Overfitting occurs when the model is not updated frequently enough with new data, leading to outdated patterns\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Overfitting occurs when the model is overly complex and captures noise or random fluctuations in the training data rather than the underlying patterns
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Overfitting happens when a model is too complex, meaning it has too many parameters relative to the number of observations. This allows the model to capture noise or random fluctuations in the training data, mistaking them for true underlying patterns, which leads to poor generalization of new data.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
