\pard\pardeftab720\sa383\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Overfitting occurs when the model is using fewer feature combinations
\f1\b0 \'a0- When the model uses fewer feature combinations, this implies that the model is simple, so it cannot overfit.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Overfitting occurs when the model ignores the training data and makes predictions based on pre-defined rules
\f1\b0 \'a0- Overfitting is about the model fitting too closely to the training data, not ignoring it.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Overfitting occurs when the model is not updated frequently enough with new data, leading to outdated patterns
\f1\b0 \'a0- While outdated data can cause poor performance, overfitting specifically refers to the model fitting the training data too well, including noise, rather than capturing general patterns.\cb1 \
