\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 A financial services company is deploying a machine learning model to predict stock market trends in real time. The model must generate predictions quickly to provide timely insights for trading decisions. The team wants to evaluate the runtime efficiency of the model to ensure it meets performance requirements.\cb1 \
\cb3 Which metric would be the most appropriate to evaluate the runtime efficiency of this model?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Model Accuracy\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Data Throughput\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 Your answer is correct
\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \strokec10 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb11 \strokec2 Average Response Time\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 Precision-Recall Score\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Average Response Time
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Average response time measures how long it takes for the model to process input data and generate a prediction. It directly reflects the model's runtime efficiency, which is crucial in scenarios where timely decisions need to be made, such as real-time stock market predictions. A lower average response time indicates better runtime efficiency, ensuring that predictions are delivered quickly enough to be actionable.\cb1 \
\cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Model Accuracy
\f1\b0 \'a0- While model accuracy is essential for assessing how well the model's predictions match the actual outcomes, it is not a measure of runtime efficiency. Accuracy evaluates the correctness of the model\'92s predictions but does not reflect how quickly those predictions are generated. For runtime efficiency, response time is the key metric, not accuracy.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Precision-Recall Score
\f1\b0 \'a0- Precision and recall are metrics used to evaluate the model's performance in handling imbalanced datasets, particularly in classification tasks. These metrics focus on the trade-off between the model\'92s ability to correctly identify positive instances and its capacity to avoid false positives. While precision-recall is important for model performance, it does not provide insights into the model's runtime efficiency.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Data Throughput
\f1\b0 \'a0- Data throughput measures the amount of data a system can process in a given time. While this can be related to the overall system performance, it does not directly assess the model's runtime efficiency in terms of how quickly it generates predictions. Average response time is a more appropriate metric for measuring runtime efficiency, particularly in real-time prediction scenarios.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
