\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 The company should create a service role for Amazon Bedrock for each team, granting access only to the specific team's clients data in Amazon S3
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 This is the correct approach because creating a service role for each team that has specific access to their data in Amazon S3 ensures fine-grained control over who can access which data. By assigning specific service roles to Amazon Bedrock, the company can enforce data security and privacy rules at the team level, ensuring that each team only has access to the data they are authorized to use. This method also aligns with AWS best practices for secure and controlled access management.\cb1 \
\cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 The company should create a single role for Amazon Bedrock with full access to Amazon S3 and then create separate IAM roles for each team that are limited to each team's clients data
\f1\b0 \'a0- This approach is incorrect because creating a single Amazon Bedrock role with full access to S3 poses a security risk, as it grants excessive permissions beyond what is necessary. Although creating separate IAM roles for each team restricts access to customer data, it does not control access at the Amazon Bedrock service level, which means that the Bedrock service could still potentially access all data in S3, defeating the purpose of limiting access.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 The company should configure S3 bucket policies to allow access to all teams but monitor usage through AWS CloudTrail logs to detect any unauthorized access
\f1\b0 \'a0- Configuring S3 bucket policies to allow broad access and relying on AWS CloudTrail logs for monitoring is a reactive approach that does not prevent unauthorized access. This method only detects and reports access violations after they occur, making it a less efficient and secure strategy for maintaining data confidentiality and access control. Proactive access management is more effective for ensuring data security.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 The company should create a single IAM policy that grants read-only access to all S3 buckets for all teams
\f1\b0 \'a0- Granting read-only access to all S3 buckets for all teams is an incorrect approach because it does not enforce data segregation or limit access to only the relevant customer data for each team. This method lacks the necessary security controls, potentially exposing sensitive data to unauthorized users and increasing the risk of data breaches.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
