\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Precision, Recall and F1-Score
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Precision, Recall, and F1-Score are standard performance metrics used to evaluate the effectiveness of a classification system:\cb1 \
\cb7 Precision: Measures the accuracy of the positive predictions, calculated as the ratio of true positives to the sum of true positives and false positives.\cb1 \
\cb7 Recall (Sensitivity): Measures the ability of the classifier to identify all positive instances, calculated as the ratio of true positives to the sum of true positives and false negatives.\cb1 \
\cb7 F1-Score: The harmonic mean of Precision and Recall, providing a single metric that balances both concerns.\cb1 \
\cb7 Metrics to measure model performance:\'a0\cb1 \
