\f1\b0 \'a0- Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), and R-squared are metrics used to evaluate regression models, not classification systems.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Throughput, Latency and Uptime
\f1\b0 \'a0- Throughput, Latency, and Uptime are performance metrics used to measure system performance and reliability, not specific to classification systems.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 Bias and Variance
\f1\b0 \'a0- Bias refers to the error introduced by approximating a real-world problem, which may be complex, with a simplified model. High bias can cause the model to miss relevant relations between features and target outputs, leading to systematic errors in predictions. Variance refers to the error introduced by the model's sensitivity to small fluctuations in the training data. High variance means the model captures noise or random fluctuations in the training data, which may not generalize well to new data. Bias and variance are not performance metrics used to evaluate classification systems.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
