\f1\b0 \'a0- An ML algorithm is not a pre-trained neural network; it is a set of mathematical instructions or procedures. The ML model is the result of training the algorithm on data.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 An ML algorithm is used for storing large datasets, whereas an ML model is used for deploying applications
\f1\b0 \'a0- ML algorithms are not used for storing datasets; they process data to create models. Models are not specifically for deploying applications but for making predictions or decisions based on the learned patterns.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 An ML algorithm is responsible for the security of the machine learning pipeline, while an ML model manages data preprocessing
\f1\b0 \'a0- The ML algorithm is not responsible for security, and the ML model does not manage data preprocessing. These tasks are part of the broader machine learning pipeline.\cb1 \
