\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 In the context of the AWS Shared Responsibility Model, which statement best describes the security responsibilities of both AWS and the customer when using Amazon Bedrock for generative AI applications?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28\fsmilli14400 \cf8 \cb9 \strokec8 Your answer is correct
\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \strokec10 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf2 \cb11 \strokec2 AWS is responsible for securing the infrastructure that runs Amazon Bedrock, while the customer is responsible for securing their data and managing access controls\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 The customer is responsible for the entire security stack, including the underlying infrastructure and the AI models\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 AWS handles all aspects of security for Amazon Bedrock, relieving the customer of any security responsibilities\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf5 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs38\fsmilli19200 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 AWS is responsible for the security of the AI models and customer data, while the customer is responsible for securing the physical infrastructure\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 \strokec2 Overall explanation
\f1 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Correct option:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 AWS is responsible for securing the infrastructure that runs Amazon Bedrock, while the customer is responsible for securing their data and managing access controls
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 According to the AWS Shared Responsibility Model, AWS manages the security of the cloud, which includes protecting the infrastructure that runs Amazon Bedrock services, such as hardware, software, networking, and facilities. Customers, on the other hand, are responsible for security in the cloud, which includes managing their data, configuring access controls, and ensuring that AI models and applications are securely implemented. For Bedrock, customers are responsible for data management, access controls, and setting up guardrails.\cb1 \
\cb7 Shared Responsibility Model Overview:\'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
