\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 Incorrect options:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 AWS is responsible for the security of the AI models and customer data, while the customer is responsible for securing the physical infrastructure
\f1\b0 \'a0- This statement incorrectly assigns physical infrastructure security to the customer. AWS secures the physical infrastructure.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 The customer is responsible for the entire security stack, including the underlying infrastructure and the AI models
\f1\b0 \'a0- This statement places too much responsibility on the customer. AWS secures the infrastructure, while the customer manages security aspects related to their data and applications.\cb1 \

\f3\b \cb7 AWS handles all aspects of security for Amazon Bedrock, relieving the customer of any security responsibilities
\f1\b0 \'a0- This statement incorrectly suggests that AWS manages all security responsibilities. The customer still has significant responsibilities, particularly around data protection and access management.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
