\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Continued Pre-training
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 In the continued pre-training process, you provide unlabeled data to pre-train a foundation model by familiarizing it with certain types of inputs. You can provide data from specific topics to expose a model to those areas. The Continued Pre-training process will tweak the model parameters to accommodate the input data and improve its domain knowledge.\cb1 \
\cb7 For example, you can train a model with private data, such as business documents, that are not publicly available for training large language models. Additionally, you can continue to improve the model by retraining the model with more unlabeled data as it becomes available.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb7 Fine-tuning
\f1\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb7 While fine-tuning a model, you provide labeled data to train a model to improve performance on specific tasks. By providing a training dataset of labeled examples, the model learns to associate what types of outputs should be generated for certain types of inputs. The model parameters are adjusted in the process and the model's performance is improved for the tasks represented by the training dataset.\cb1 \
